Tom: I''ve heard of him. He tried to cross Antarctica, didn''t he?
Lily: Yes, but his ship got stuck in the ice and was crushed before it sank.
Tom: So he never reached the land he planned to cross?
Lily: No, he failed to reach his goal. But the wonderful thing is that he brought every man home alive.
Tom: Every single one? After the ship was lost?
Lily: That''s right. They lived on the ice for almost two years. People remember him for his leadership, not for winning.
Tom: Now I really want to read that book too.', 'Lily 刚读完关于沙克尔顿的书,说他是了不起的探险家;Tom 知道他想横穿南极;Lily 说他的船被冰困住、压碎后沉没,目标没达成,但了不起的是把全员活着带回;船在冰上漂了近两年;人们记住他是因为领导力而非成功;Tom 也想读这本书。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Shackleton trying to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Cross Antarctica.","Sail around the world.","Reach the moon.","Build a whaling station."]},{"q":"What happened to his ship?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It safely returned home.","It was crushed by the ice and sank.","It was sold to another country.","It is still sailing today."]},{"q":"Did he reach the land he planned to cross?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["No, he failed to reach his goal.","Yes, easily.","Yes, but very late.","He never tried."]},{"q":"What is the amazing thing about the story?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He found gold on the ice.","He brought every man home alive.","He finished in a single week.","He travelled completely alone."]},{"q":"Why do people remember Shackleton?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["For being the fastest sailor.","For staying at home safely.","For his leadership rather than for winning.","For giving up early."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U3', 'sufe');
Ben: Maybe, but it takes a lot of planning. You can''t just set out.
Anna: What do I need to learn first?
Ben: You should learn to read maps and to understand the weather. Storms can appear without warning.
Anna: That sounds frightening. How do explorers stay warm?
Ben: They use special clothing and strong tents made for the cold. And modern teams carry radios.
Anna: So they can call for rescue if something goes wrong?
Ben: Exactly. But careful planning still matters as much as courage. You should train for months before you go.', 'Anna 想有朝一日参加极地探险,问能否做到;Ben 说可能,但需要大量准备,不能贸然出发;Anna 问先学什么;Ben 说要会看地图、懂天气,因为风暴会突然来;探险者靠特制衣物和耐寒帐篷保暖,现代队伍还带无线电;Anna 问出事能否求救;Ben 说能,但谨慎规划与勇气同样重要,出发前要训练数月。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Anna want to do one day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Join a polar expedition.","Open a clothing shop.","Become a weather reporter.","Sail around a warm island."]},{"q":"What does Ben say she must do first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy a wooden ship.","Learn to read maps and understand the weather.","Travel completely alone.","Forget about planning."]},{"q":"Why is the weather so important?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is always sunny at the poles.","Rain makes the trip easier.","Storms can appear without warning.","Weather never changes there."]},{"q":"How do modern teams keep safe?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They go without any clothing.","They never bring tents.","They avoid all training.","They use warm gear and carry radios."]},{"q":"What matters as much as courage, according to Ben?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Careful planning.","Travelling fast.","Skipping training.","Going alone."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U3', 'sufe');
Kate: Keep moving, then. If we sit still too long, we''ll get too cold.
Sam: I know. How far is it to the station now?
Kate: About sixty kilometres, over the mountains. No one has crossed here on foot before.
Sam: And we have no tent. We can''t really stop to sleep, can we?
Kate: No. If we fall asleep in this cold, we might never wake up.
Sam: Then let''s keep marching. Thinking of the others waiting for us helps me go on.
Kate: Same for me. Come on, the sooner we reach help, the sooner we can save them.', 'Sam 说今夜极冷,手都快没知觉;Kate 让他保持活动,坐太久会冻坏;Sam 问到站点还有多远;Kate 说约六十公里、要翻山,此前无人徒步穿越;Sam 说他们没帐篷,不能真正停下睡觉;Kate 说不能,在这种冷里睡着可能再也醒不来;Sam 说那就继续行进,想到等待的伙伴就有动力;Kate 也一样,越快求到援助,越快能去救他们。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Kate tell Sam to keep moving?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Walking is more fun than resting.","The path is too crowded.","Sitting still too long will make them too cold.","She wants to win a race."]},{"q":"How far is it to the station?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only a few steps away.","Six hundred kilometres by boat.","They do not know at all.","About sixty kilometres over the mountains."]},{"q":"Why can''t they stop to sleep?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They might never wake up in the cold.","They are not tired at all.","The station closes at night.","They left their tent behind on purpose."]},{"q":"What gives Sam the strength to go on?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The hope of finding gold.","Thinking of the others waiting for help.","The warm weather ahead.","A reward of money."]},{"q":"Why does Kate want to reach help quickly?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["So they can rest on a beach.","So they can go shopping.","So they can save the others sooner.","So they can sail home alone."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U3', 'sufe');

